    "mandatory": true,
    "audit_trail": null,
    "ai_match_reasoning": "Our extraction answered \"Yes\" because materai (Rp 10,000 stamp) is present on the contract. That's correct — materai exists. But materai is standard on virtually ALL Indonesian agreements; it's just a revenue stamp. The \"Registered\" part asks whether the agreement was formally registered with government authorities, which is a separate legal step most lease agreements DON'T go through"
  },
